A one-way push on your own initiative, no reply expected. Only server → client and microservice → parent server; the reverse directions go through REQ. An announcement that arrived for you → `sdh-cross-repo-announce-read`.

## 0. Is it an announcement?

| Situation | Channel |
|---|---|
| The recipient asked for X and you did it | REQ receipt (`sdh-cross-repo-req-answer`) |
| Your own change affects the recipient | announcement |
| Work for recipient A has a side effect on B | announcement to B |
| An internal rework forces the recipient's integration to adjust | announcement |
| The recipient's REQ was closed (✓) before you shipped it | announcement — it is now the release receipt (threshold below does not apply) |

Threshold: write one only if the recipient must change code, config or behaviour, or acknowledge a deprecation. A new endpoint they may adopt later reaches them through the contract sync.

## 1. Recipient path — from your `docs/project.md`

| Direction | Path column | Where you write |
|---|---|---|
| Server → client | `## Repositories`, rows with role `client` / `admin_client` / `test_client` | `<client-path>/docs/server-announcements/<your-repo>/ANNOUNCE-NNN_<slug>.md` |
| Microservice → parent | `## Parent projects`, row of the target server | `<parent-path>/docs/microservice-announcements/<your-ms-project>/ANNOUNCE-NNN_<slug>.md` |

No path (`_no local path configured_`) or `⚠ server repo not resolvable` → do not write; tell the user or file a `T-` task. Folder names use the last segment (`web-app-backend`); take yours from the `## Repositories` row whose path is the current directory.

## 2. Number

Per sender × recipient pair, monotonic, never reused. Folder absent → create it, `001`. Otherwise `max + 1` — but acknowledged announcements are deleted, so also check the recipient's records (`docs/done.md`, commits, specs) for higher numbers.

## 3. File

```markdown
# ANNOUNCE-NNN: <headline>

## Why this matters to you
<impact on the recipient>

## What changed
<the change on your side>

## What you need to do
<steps: integration / migration / acknowledgement>

## References
- <commit / endpoint>
```

You write it directly into the recipient's repo and keep no copy; its git history is the record. No registry in this channel.

This direct write is the one exception to "never write across a repo boundary", and it holds only for these two vertical directions. Between equals you write only in your own repo (`sdh-peer-channel-send`). The app does not track announcements; the recipient deletes the file once applied.
